# Build the Deal Stack — Project Rules for Cursor AI

This project is a third‑party, transactional readiness simulator for Nigerian real estate.
It is NOT a game platform but a **qualification funnel** to identify serious buyers and investors.

Tech Stack:
- HTML5, CSS3, and vanilla JavaScript (ES6+)
- No JavaScript frameworks
- Local Storage for state persistence
- Three pages: index.html, game.html, result.html
- Modular JS files: js/data.js, js/state.js, js/rules.js, js/game.js, js/result.js

General Conventions:
- Use clear and descriptive variable and function names
- Break large functions into smaller reusable helpers
- Avoid global variables unless intentionally shared state
- Wrap Local Storage access in helper functions
- Keep DOM manipulation minimal and readable

UX & Language Guidance:
- Use professional, investment‑ready tone
- Avoid playful or gamification language
- Terms like “Transaction Readiness Score”, “Required Steps”, “Deal Health”, “Risk Indicators” are preferred
- Do NOT use words such as “points”, “badges”, “win”, “game”, or “level”

Rules Engine Expectations:
- The rules engine must:
  - Confirm presence of mandatory cards
  - Validate correct sequencing
  - Apply penalties for wrong order or missing steps
  - Compute a Transaction Readiness Score (TRS) between 0–100
- TRS bands:
  - TRS >= 80 → high readiness
  - 65 <= TRS < 80 → moderate readiness
  - TRS < 65 → low readiness

Local Storage State:
- Session state should be stored as a single object
- Encapsulate saves and loads
- Do not store sensitive user data
- The session must survive page reloads without backend

Drag‑and‑Drop UI:
- Use HTML5 native drag and drop
- Prevent duplicate card placement
- Update risk and time indicators in real time on stack changes

Result Page Logic:
- Read TRS from Local Storage
- Render score and explanatory feedback
- Select appropriate CTA based on TRS band
- Do not refer to “games” or “scores” in CTA copy

Edge Cases:
- Empty stack submission must show advisory feedback
- Mandatory cards missing must trigger inline explanatory dialog
- Reset functionality must clear Local Storage state and restart

Always follow the above conventions when generating code, fixing bugs, or creating new features.

